{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1386630-actual-play-oklahoma-demons-session-1","id":1386630,"title":"Actual Play: Oklahoma Demons, Session 1","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T00:19:14-07:00","id":1386630,"title":"Actual Play: Oklahoma Demons, Session 1","content":"I'm not sure the best way to post this - my DtD chronicle is <a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615\" target=\"_blank\">available online</a> as is the<a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/notes/26185\" target=\"_blank\"> session below. </a> But I thought that I might post the text here as well. <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon Tzengeti: Professor of Anthropology<br /> Lexis Staiffer: Young indie rocker <br /> Zachariah Ross: Small business lawyer<br /> Reginald Waters: Therapist<br /> Jennifer Reddings: Freelance museum assistant<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Backstory: </b> Norman Oklahoma, houses a major GM Infrastructure, the National Weather Center. Previous attempts to infiltrate or sabotage it have been met with overwhelming devastation (e.g. the world record May 1999 tornado outburst). An Agency (&quot;The Damned Few&quot;) decided that a small Ring of &quot;younger&quot; Demons would be assigned to monitor the Weather Center, but not interfere with it. However, unexpected developments will lead the players to a different mission....<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Ring gather for their regular meeting at the Wafflehouse, a safe screened location. Solomon goes to the standard dead-drop, a newspaper vending machine. In response to his putting the appropriate coins in, the vending machine door opens to reveal a cell-phone and a large manila envelope. He retrieves them and joins the Ring back at the table.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The phone rings - it is Mr. Gone, their appointed contact with The Damned Few. Something odd is going on Eastern Oklahoma. He explains the images in the envelope. </span><ul><li>&quot;Missing 411 Map:&quot; Some of these disappearances are due to recognized groups: <i>The Cult of 17 </i>out West, the <i>DreamEaters</i> of the Northwest, and a variety of GM harvesting operations. However there is a cluster of unexplained activity in Eastern Oklahoma. Several have happened over the last few years, but there is now a spike in disappearances.</li> <li>Local news reports tell of cattle mutilations that indicate something odd as well - possibly cryptids.</li> <li>There have been recent disappearances near Talking Trees Camp Ground. Normally this woud be covered more widely. The lack of coverage indicates active suppression of news coverage.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\">The major GM Facility is at the Weather Center, and it is well observed. However, it appears that there is some <i>other</i> major GM operation going on where none was expected. This alone is very disturbing. <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The PC's are being moved from their observing mission to investigate the source of the disappearances in Eastern Oklahoma. If it <i>is</i> cryptids, that means Aether which means GM activity. However, the GM also hunts cryptids, both to prevent discovery and as possible Demon hunters. So caution is advised.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The PC's make moderate preparations; those with appropriate firearm skills pack theirs along. They all climb in to Zach's car and drive two and half hours east to the Talking Trees campground, which was now closed and up for sale.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">At the parking lot to the campground there are two separate groups already there, and preparing to head out. The first group is a pair of local hunters, Jeb and Boone, who have heard the stories of some &quot;critter&quot; haunting the woods and have come to investigate and, they hope, get a story worthy of telling over beer. The second group is assembled next to their Bigfoot Hunters truck. The group of four consists of the stars of the former TV show <i>BigFoot Hunters, </i>Bobby Brewster and his older brother Ray, the camera man Mario Santos, and the driver and handyman Lou Weber. The show <i>Bigfoot Hunters</i> ran for a year, and while it initially was quite popular, viewership fell as it became clear that they never found Bigfoot. After their series was cancelled, the Brewsters hope to start a new show with a wider focus on general &quot;Unseen America&quot;. They had heard about something interesting in Eastern Oklahoma from their sources on the internet and decided to check it out.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Lexis Staiffer quickly insinuated herself with the TV crew, acting the gushing fan. A few good social rolls later and she and Jennifer went along to fan out with the crew and look for signs of anything paranormal. Solomon and Zach paired off with Jeb and Boone, with Solomon attempting the <i>Cause and Effect</i> embed to drive the two groups together so that they could be more easily managed and/or protected. A dramatic failure gave the ST some dice to use when least convenient. Reginald Waters stayed behind in the parking lot to do more investigation, which turned out to be a lucky decision.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Shortly after the two hunting groups had departed a <i>third</i> group showed up. They arrived in three pick-up trucks and gave off an air of severe purpose. Six of them looked the part of hard working farming types packing a distressing amount of firepower. Two of them were noticeably odd: large, bull-necked bodybuilders, clad only in blue jean pants. Shirtless, shoeless and wearing dark sunglasses, they leapt from the trucks with cat-like easy, carrying pieces of steel rebar, wielding them like <i>jo</i> sticks. The party of eight trotted off into the woods at a rapid clip. Waters texted the others about their arrival.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The two groups spread out into the woods. Solomon tried to persuade Jeb and Boone to meet up with the Bigfoot Hunters (2 Doors, 10 minutes/attempt) and eventually succeeded. As they headed for the other party the heard a scream....<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Bigfoot Hunters plus Demons had fanned out through the woods looking for anything unusual. Lexis Staiffer had seen something obscured in the bushes - a body. It was at least two days old and had not been gnawed so much as <i>abraded</i> in parts, as if someone had taken a grinder to it in spots and rasped off the flesh. Suddenly the world seemed to go off balance and disorienting, a feeling of vertigo swept through everyone (human) as a scream rang out. <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Some <i>thing</i> had leapt on the back of Bobby Brewster. Its large insectile eyes, each the size of an outstretched hand, were expressionless and its mandibles shredded through the base of Bobby's neck and into his skull. The hornet-like head was mounted on chitinous armored shoulders that were themselves the front part of something large and bear-shaped. A horrible monstrosity with the body of a bear, yet with the head of insect and small, vestigial forearms that shifted Bobby's corpse slightly to better feed.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">There were more screams and now shouts. The vertigo added to the sense of unreality and confusion. Waters fired his pistol at the beast but its bulk absorbed the shot without any apprarent reaction. Jennifer improvised a club from a stick, and Alexis used an Embed to distract the beast away into the woods - nearly sending it directly into the path of the incoming party of Solomon <i>et al.</i> (those dice from the above dramatic failure almost made this much more complicated...). Lexis then caught sight of a second beast approaching from the brush as well. The PC's decided that a strategic retreat was necessary.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The redneck cavalry arrived. One muscular, bare-chested attacker smashed the skull of the Hive Bear with an iron bar, spraying blood and ichor. The PC's tried to get Ray, Mario and Lou away from the scene, but with great difficulty. Mario did his best to keep filming and had to be abandoned. After several shots were fired the sounds of battle died down. The PCs saw Mario arguing with one of heavily armed victors. The gentleman wanted Mario's camera and was prepared to take it at gunpoint. When Mario continued to object, one of the muscular figures put him in a Full Nelson. The PC's rapidly ran for the parking lot, but could still make out the rattling <i>crack</i> of vertebrae as the argument behind them was finally concluded.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon invoked an Embed to read Jeb before he also fled the scene, searching for a recent source of sorrow. He read that Jeb was thinking about the heavily armed posse that they were fleeing: &quot;I wish someone would tell off those assholes from The Farm - they push everyone around.&quot; <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The PC's decided it was time to rapidly depart.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:29:47-07:00","id":1387331,"title":"","content":"I really like the Bigfoot Hunters. A good hook for the players. <br /> <br /> The Weather Station sounds like it should be an awesome session when they get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:04:26-07:00","id":1387389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1386630-actual-play-oklahoma-demons-session-1?p=1387331#post1387331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the Bigfoot Hunters. A good hook for the players.<br /> <br /> The Weather Station sounds like it should be an awesome session when they get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the feedback. When you post something like this, you never know if any reads it all. <br /> <br /> Ray Brewster will show up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:16:06-07:00","id":1387393,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/notes/26584\" target=\"_blank\">Link to campaign website</a><br /> <br /> <u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon Tzengeti<br /> Lexis Staiffer<br /> Zachariah Ross<br /> Reginald Waters<br /> Jennifer Reddings</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Ring decided to hole up in a hotel room, investigate what the could via phone and internet, and make plans for the next day.</span><ul><li>Lexis recalled the tattoos on one of the muscular attackers. She determined that it was a corruption of an emblem of the Knights Templar, where the crosses had been replaced by gears. It also had the initials &quot;DMV&quot; in gothic font added to the top, where the traditional emblem would have had <i>Deus Vult </i>(&quot;God Wills It&quot;).</li> <li>Solomon used his hacking Savant Core to determine that this logo was connected to WatchMaker publications, and in particular their series of pamphlets entitled <i>Divine Designs.</i> These are aimed an Christians interested in Intelligent Design and transhumanism. The address of the publisher is listed as Elohim City. It is a small press, only recently in business. He expresses enthusiasm for finding some way to hack into their system.</li> <li>Reginald learns from his police contacts that the plates of the redneck cavalry are registered to residents in Elohim City, about 90 minutes north of Talking Trees. No criminal record. Elohim City was founded by a conservative religious Christian group and is small and insular. It's close to the border with Arkansas so jurisdiction can get murky. Vague concerns about white supremacists, but the Feds would have more information about that. Local sheriff is Arnold Bryant. He has a reputation of being a straight-shooter, no nonsense type.</li> <li>Jennifer learns from her Contact (Cryptic Expert) the there must be a major source or cache of Aether within a mile or so radius of where they encountered them. Cryptids need it to maintain their unnatural existence. She also suggests that Jennifer be careful - these critters probably need a lot of Aether and the PCs are a source for them.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\">This information round-up took hours, and then the Ring talked late into the night. Should they stay in the area and try to figure out the cryptic issue, or follow the leads to Elohim City? How dangerous would it be to do one task versus the other? After some wrangling and indecision the Ring opted to at least drive through Elohim City, and get a general feeling for what it was like. The piled in to Zachariah's black SUV and headed ninety minutes north.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Elohim City is a bump on an interstate road. The highway slows down to 35mph for a bit and then there is a single stoplight at the center of town surrounded by a half a dozen buildings. The light marks a T-junction. The street comes off the highway, and then forms a \u201cU\u201d, connecting back a further bit down the way. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A quick glance shows a gas station, a roadside restaurant, antique and hardware stores, a larger corrugated building set back a bit from the road, and a city hall. There are a dozen or so houses as well, and one can see a church steeple, set a block or so further away from the highway. It gave the players an overall impression of a run-down, hick town that must be boring to stop at and soul-destroying to live in. A moments reflection revealed that these feels were being projected, radiated by some sort of Concealment Infrastructure. Furthermore, the city layout did not match the satellite images from Google maps, at all. Something is being hidden here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The PCs drive through town and out the other side, and then start on <i>another</i> long discussion on what to do next. They decided that after their long discussion it was safe to turn around and stop in the gas station and get a bite to eat. Solomon would look for wifi to hack, while Lexis would get take-out from Cassidy's, the diner.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Lexis enters the diner and is told by Marylou, a stereotypical diner waitress, that they don't do take out. As she tries to text the others to this effect, a tall homeless man shambles in. Marylou berates the man (who she calls &quot;Bear&quot;) and sends him on his way, while Lexis is puzzled to find that her phone does not seem to work. It a few moments it seems to be restored and she texts and Jennifer comes to join them. Jennifer crosses the street to join Lexis and runs into Bear. He goes on a rambling tirade on how the farm isn't a farm, that there should be &quot;no blood for oil,&quot; and that they &quot;plan to blow up Spain!&quot;. Jennifer politely excused herself and joined Lexis. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cassidy\u2019s Cafe is a slightly run down diner with a Western theme. There\u2019s a front counter with six stools and standard soda fountain and diner fare. There are booths and a jukebox as well. On one wall there is a long mural on showing an old time saloon. It\u2019s a big garish but well done. There is a jukebox that plays vinyl 45\u2019s, which is a bit unusual. The waitress was in her late 40\u2019s and seemed chipper when she offered coffee. Someone puts a coin in the jukebox, and you hear Chubby Checkers, telling people to \u201cDo the Twist.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon, Zachariah, and Reginald are still at the gas station. There is much discussion on what to do next. Solomon searches for wifi, but gets nothing. They decide that it would be a good idea to triangulate on the Concealment Infrastructure that is radiating the feeling that deters visitors.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Back at the diner, Lexis and Jennifer enjoy lunch. Tthe same patron goes to the jukebox and plays it again, in exactly the same motions. The other patrons move their food around but don\u2019t eat much. The same coffee and food orders keep getting placed and repeated. Solomon, Zachariah, and Reginald move the car in front of the diner and join them. Solomon explains that he wants to put on a charade of having lost his wallet so that they have an excuse to wander the streets. Jennifer &quot;decides&quot; that she really would like to have dessert; Lexis gets suspicious and decides to stay with her. She and Jennifer decide to have some pie and someone again plays Chubby Checkers, who again tells everyone to &quot;Do The Twist.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Lexis examines the place more carefully. The pie is certainly tasty, and she asks the waitress for the recipe. It does seem to be a nice place to sit and rest. While the waitress writes it down, someone again plays the same song on the jukebox. Lexis notices that each of the patrons in the diner appear in some fashion in the mural: the waitress, some of the people at the tables, and painted at one table in the mural is the small figure of Jennifer, and a ghostly image that is looking more and more like herself. She uses some Manipulation+Persuasion to finally get get Jennifer to leave. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Meanwhile, Solomon, Zachariah, and Reginald each walk in a separate direction to triangulate. Zachariah notices a young teen-age girl waving imploringly at him from the porch of her house. She seems to be urging him to join her on the porch. Zachariah ignored her and moved on. Reginald encountered Bear during his walk and heard the same sort of ravings as had Jennifer. The three Demons determined that the Concealment Infrastructure is in the old church, just a block or so away from the highway. They meet back up and the group decides to investigate. They drive to the church and park. Lexis remains behind the wheel and waits.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The &quot;True Gospel Church&quot; is a moderate wooden structure (small for a church) that dated from the 1920\u2019s. Its spire is visible from the highway, but it is back a few blocks. Closer inspection revealed that the church is largely abandoned. The windows are broken, and mostly boarded up. There were 2x4\u2019s across the entrance. Zach uses his Embed &quot;Like I Built It&quot; to find a way into the church, and the four Demons climbed up through a low broken window. They found much of it destroyed inside, with the letters &quot;DMV&quot; in paint slathered on the walls in oddly luminous paint. Zach guided the players up to the bell in the church tower. It was connected to brass gears at odd angles and clearly part of the Infrastructure. Close inspection revealed that the clapper was the Linchpin. It was wrapped in a skin bag stuffed with human hair. It would \u201cring\u201d every 23 minutes, sending out a signal that persuades people that there is nothing interesting here. Zachariah crushed the bag and it vanished in a cloud of black sparks. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">While those in the church congratulated themselves on their victory, a police car pulled up behind Lexis, who was parked outside the church. The sheriff stepped out of the car and approached her....</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24502,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","user":"KieranMullen","date":".  Added link to campaign website 05-11-2020, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T19:51:28-07:00","id":1390898,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/notes/28263\" target=\"_blank\">Link to campaign website.</a></i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 783px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Name</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Virtue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Vice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Aspirations</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Solomon Tzengeti</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Make contact with the cultist,</li> <li>Find a mortal who doesn't deserve Joy</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Lexis Staiffer</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Ambitious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Arrogant</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Release a full length album,</li> <li>Play to 50+ people.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Zachariah Ross (Mr. Zets)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Patient</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build something.</li> <li>Experience the loss of something.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Reginald Waters (EM)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Establish a 2nd cover.;.</li> <li>Kiss a random person -</li> <li>Live life to the fullest;</li> <li>Contribute a positive action to the team.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Jennifer Reddings (Query)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Thorough</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Break into the publishing house,</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\">As Solomon, Leix, Zachariah and Jennifer completed the destruction of the Infrastructure linchpin in the church bell tower, Lexis waited for them in their rented SUV. Behind her, a police car had pulled up and parked. A sheriff got out, every inch the southern, mirror-shaded nightmare an out-of-town motorist might fear. Lexis, thinking quickly, activated her <i>Special Message</i> embed, and whistled a happy tune, tapping out a syncopated rhythm with her hand on the door. (<b>&quot;Don't leave the church</b>&quot;) </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">There was just a tinge of menace in his voice as he spoke: &quot;Pardon me, Missy, kehn I halp you?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The four in the church belfry scanned the scene. However, they soon had their own problem - the sound of someone downstairs moving around in the abandoned church. It was clear that whoever or whatever was downstairs, it would soon be coming up. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">As Lexis started to make small talk with the sheriff, a familiar figure lurched between them - it was the homeless man who had she had seen trying to enter the diner earlier that day. Barging between the between Lexis and the sheriff, he leaned in through the window of the SUV, brought his scraggly face close to Lexis. Their eyes, met, and his seemed momentarily lucid. He whispered to her <i>&quot;Run.&quot; </i> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">As the demons in the church readied themselves Mr. Zets flicked a cigarette out of the belltower and activated a <i>Cause and Effect</i> embed to produce a car crash to distract the sheriff. EM activated his <i>Sonic Acuity</i> Form ability. His ears faded away, leaving an odd grey, fuzzy emptiness on either side of his head. He could hear the approach of someone climbing the stairs. He focussed on the sounds of their approach, the slap of their bare feet, the pounding of their heart and rapid breath. It was a young teen-ager, probably a young girl. He motioned to the others to stand down. A young, blond girl poked her head in: &quot;You four don't have the sense God gave a headless chicken!&quot; She urged them to follow her down the stairs and away from the church. Mr. Zets could sense no menace in her motives and the four followed her down the stairs, and out of the back of the church through a loose board in a back wall.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Outside, the homeless man got into an altercation with the sheriff, drawing both of them away from Lexis. The sheriff drawled &quot;Bear, you ain't the sheriff around here no more!,&quot; and gut-punched the taller man, sending him to the pavement. As he proceeded to boot the helpless man, Lexis started the SUV and pulled away. She rapidly returned to the highway, and drove for a mile before she found a place she could hide the rented truck, out of sight of the highway.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Meanwhile the four demons were lead by back-alleys to a run-down house nearby. The house itself, while not a disaster, was in poor shape and decidedly messy inside. The girl introduced herself as Marcy-May Beeman - but she goes by &quot;Mac&quot;. Her five year old brother Bobby joined them clutching a blanket and stared at them blankly. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Mac explained that she had seen them wandering around town and didn't want them to &quot;disappear like the others.&quot; She knew that she had to get them off the streets, especially after she saw that they had been messing about with the church. She explained that things had not always been so bad, that people from &quot;The Farm&quot; were always a bit gun-crazy and paranoid, but that in the last year or two things had gotten completely out-of-hand. The change had happened with the arrival of the publishing company that moved in to town, and their evangelical work on &quot;God's new creation.&quot; The Farm community got much more menacing, had chased out the local pastor and many of the businesses, which drove many townspeople away. Most of the people who remained were either part of the company, The Farm, or simply couldn't leave.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon asked about Mac's family. She explained that her father had died a long time ago, and that her mother... she was at a loss for words. Bobby asked where their mother was and Mac shushed him. Her explanation was interrupted by a figure that came to the door. Mac gestured to the Demons to relax and do nothing. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">In walked Marylou, from Cassidy's Cafe, in her waitressing uniform. Bobby cried out &quot;Momma!&quot;, but Mac held him too her side and cautioned in a low voice, &quot;That ain't Momma no more.&quot; Marylou Beeman took one look at the four strangers in her house, smiled and said &quot;I'll go get you some menus. Can I bring you back anything to drink? Coffee?&quot;. The demons exchanged glances, and ordered their drinks. Marylou took their orders and went back out the door. Bobby snuffled tears into Mac's side.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Mac explained that shortly after working at Cassidy's her mother had changed. All she was, and all she did was be a waitress. Mac wasn't even sure her mother (or what she was now) even slept. She didn't recognize Mac or Bobby, but treated them as customers. Mac had turned this to there advantage, having her mother &quot;charge her tab&quot; to &quot;her mother.&quot; So waitress Marylou's wages paid for Mac and Bobby's food. Mac offered to help if the four of them would get Bobby and her out of town and some place safe. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Lexis was working her way through the woods. Moving with a modicum of stealth, she avoided a pair of men patrolling the forest in camouflage carrying rifles. Quietly she headed back to the town and the church, hoping to rejoin the others. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">At the same time, Reginald decided to work his way back to the church as well, remembering Mac's circuitous path as best he could. However, he got called out by an old woman as he tried to sneak through her backyard. A feisty sort, she reached for her shotgun and fired in his direction, but between her rheumy eyes and his fast feet she missed him entirely. However, the sound of the blast was bound to bring the police soon. <i>(Dramatic Failure).</i> Luckily, he and Lexis met up, and soon they were heading for the SUV. They retrieved the vehicle and drove back to pick up the others, perhaps foolishly driving the same SUV that the sheriff had noticed Lexis in earlier. Although the seven piled rapidly into the car they had not escaped the police. As they pulled away a police car flashed its lights and prepared to pursue.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Only to be front-ended by a car that had swerved to avoid a squirrel carrying the cigarette from Zet's <i>Cause and Effect </i>embed from earlier in the session!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Game Mechanics Notes:<br /> EM spent 2 Aether activating and deactivating his form ability. He avoided Compromise, but picked up a Condition.<br /> Solomon and Query regained full Willpower (Virture: Curious)<br /> Lexis gained a Beat for her using her music in a clever fashion, and full Willpower by handling the sheriff on her own.<br /> Reginald gained a beat for contributing to the team.<br /> Everyone gains one beat and one experience. </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24502,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","user":"KieranMullen","date":".  Added link to the campaign website. 05-23-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T18:06:03-07:00","id":1392085,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/notes/28583\" target=\"_blank\">Link to Campaign site</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 783px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Name</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Virtue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Vice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Aspirations</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Solomon Tzengeti</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Make contact with the cultist,</li> <li>Protect a ring mate</li> <li>debate a cultist,</li> <li>work on secondary cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Lexis Staiffer</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Ambitious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Arrogant</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Release a full length album,</li> <li>Play to 50+ people.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Zachariah Ross (Mr. Zets)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Patient</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build something.</li> <li>Experience the loss of something.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Reginald Waters (EM)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Establish a 2nd cover;</li> <li>Protect/defend ring mate on Cryptid mission.;</li> <li>Contribute to success of overall mission.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Jennifer Reddings (Query)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Thorough</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build and use a new tool,</li> <li>Break into the publishing house,</li> <li>Bring an intact but disconnected piece of Infrastructure home for study</li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Ring drove north of town, to Heavner, and found a hotel for the night. Solomon pumped Marcy May Beeman for information, but while she was cooperative, she could not give him the details of the operations of The Farm (times of patrols, etc.) that he wanted. She explained that the local police were in cahoots with the cultists and that those who did not join the cult were chased out of town. The only people left were too old or too poor to leave. Eventually Solomon planned to make a Pact with her - she would give up her childhood in Elohim City in return for a secure foster home for her and her brother, Bobby. <i>(Greater, Permanent, for Resources, Mentor and Safe House). </i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> There was much, much discussion about what to do next. Should the Ring pursue their original investigation of the cryptid's further south, and find out their true origin? Or should they pursue the GodMachine activity they had found in Elohim City? The two were clearly related, since the posse that killed the cryptids was from Elohim City. It was suggested that maybe the Ring could lure a Hive Bear from Talking Trees Camp Ground in the south up to The Farm thereby causing confusion and perhaps destruction. However they judged it impractical to lure a Hive Bear nearly ninety miles (145km) in any reasonable amount of time. After more discussion the Ring decided to break into Watchmaker Publicationsand see what they could find.<br /> <br /> Zets was assigned to stay with Mac and Bobby <i>(Player late to session)</i>, while the other four drove back to the edge of town. The Ring had decided that since the building had few windows and the front door was visible from the street, they would try to enter through the loading dock at the rear of the building. Lexis's bump of direction allowed her to lead them through the woods to the back of the parking lot of the publishing company. There Jennifer was able sense <i>(Like I Built It embed)</i> gave her a sense of the building. Rather than finding an opening through which to teleport and risk Compromise and use up Aether, Jennifer tried to pick the lock, <i>(Right Tools </i><i>embed). </i>The Ring got in with no problems.<br /> <br /> The Ring entered the building to find that the majority of it was taken up with a few printing presses, pallets of paper, and cartons of printed books and pamphlets. The printing presses and printed materials registered faintly when Jennifer spent Aether on Aetheric Resonance. She determined that it was imbued with a faint effect that rendered the reader more receptive to the materials printed, and the effect came from the ink used.<br /> <br /> At the front of the building were the offices, set off from the rest by partitions and a drop ceiling. Jennifer again picked the lock and the Ring cautiously entered the reception area of the front office. This would be where the secretary/receptionist for the office would sit, and her work area included a desk, computer and file cabinets. There was a locked door off this area that lead to a second office. It bore the name plate inscribed &quot;Lyle Smith, Manager.&quot;<br /> <br /> The lock on this door was more tricky, and in picking it Query actually broke the lock. <i>(Dramatic Failure). </i>They inspected the office ceilings are realized that if they were careful they could lift Lexis up through the drop ceiling over the partition walls so that she could drop into the office. After a brief scramble she was able to open the door from the inside and let the players in.<br /> <br /> Solomon smiled, sat in front of the computer, and got to work. Gold dust glittered in front of his eyes, forming wires that connected him to the machine. Activating his Savant Core hacking skills, he sucked up all the information he could. He scanned through some of it, and sent the rest to cloud storage via his phone. The computing system was fairly simple, and not connected to the internet - only the two office computers were connected, and that was by a hard wire. Emails were handled via the phone lines, indicating an odd lack of connection to the outside world.<br /> <br /> Lexis looked around the office and found a map of Oklahoma stretched out on the desk. There were numerous small markings and numerical notation written in precise handwriting at many locations. But what caught her eye were the three lines that ran across the map and crossed in northeastern Oklahoma. The occult notation about them indicated that they were ley lines, lines of occult power. &quot;I'm definitely going to take <i>this!&quot; </i>she exclaimed.<br /> <br /> Reginald sifted through the paperwork in the office and checked with Solomon and several facts were clear. First, this operation was a small one. It had only been in operation for about 18 months, and its reach extended through parts of the central U.S. but no further. The operation did not have they pyramid scheme for some sort of exponential proselytizing growth, but seemed to be targeted. However, it was intense. GodMachine activity was hard on cultists since exposure to Essence and Aether had unhealthy effects. (The odd form of the Weathermen was proof of that.) For this reason cults were often carefully groomed with lots of lower level members who could be promoted as more senior ones became too damaged to be useful. This operation was anomalous in its ruthless exploitation of cult members. <br /> <br /> The Ring continued to search for the <i>purpose</i> of the operation. It was clear that The Farm was producing something for an occult matrix. There were notations of gallons produced, and some sort of calendar that referenced phases of the moon. What was going on?<br /> <br /> Solomon sifted through the emails looking for a clue. One caught his eye:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><i>To: <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#91e2fcf8e5f9d1e6f0e5f2f9fcf0faf4e3e1e4f3bff2fefc\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"6b1806021f032b1c0a1f0803060a000e191b1e0945080406\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><i>From: <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#420a10022123302e203730362d2c6c212d2f\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"551d071536342739372027213a3b7b363a38\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><i>Dear Lyle,</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><i>While I have been informed that we have enough resources from your Farm to implement the project, it would be prudent to increase our supply to give us a safety margin. Please continue production and shipping as per usual.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><i>Parenthetically, She Who Must Not Be Named has asked me to relay to you that she will not brook any interference with her people. Just because their trucks are government property is no reason for your flock to give them grief. So let\u2019s keep your useful idiots from destroying her useful idiots, shall we?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><i>This whole project has been an interesting experiment. Shame that will end soon.</i></span><br /> <br /> Bingo! A connection to someone up the chain. This would give them new avenues to research.<br /> <br /> It was soon time to leave. The were concerned about leaving a broken lock as a trace of their break-in. Jennifer suggested that given time, she might be able to fix the lock in a fashion that there would be no trace of tampering. <i>(Extended Action, with assistance rolls from Solomon, plus Right Tools embed). </i>Satisfied that no one could detect that they had picked the lock, the Ring exited the office, locking all doors behind them. On the way out Query snagged one of the jugs of Essence imbued ink - you never know if that might come in handy. Rather than sneak out the back door, the Ring elected to each use their <i>Teleport</i> Form abilities. They simply had to find clear sight to a point at the edge of the woods an invoke their ability. From there the trip back to the SUV was uneventful. <br /> <br /> They returned to the hotel and discussed their findings with Zets. Solomon concluded his pact with Mac Beeman, and they all turned in for the night. In the morning Solomon found an message in his email from State Foster Services dating from last week. The email thanked him for his temporary fostering of the Beeman children and stated that they would be picked up in two days from his own residence.<br /> <br /> The Ring returned to Norman and shored up their Covers, contacting their co-workers and loved ones, and putting in some hours at their jobs. Zets on entering his office one morning found an interesting pamphlet from Watchmaker Publications on his desk. His secretary explained that it had been dropped off by a nice silver haired old man who had attempted to sell her a fine family Bible....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Solomon gets a Beat for his secondary Cover Aspiration.<br /> Query gets two Beats for their Aspirations. <br /> Everyone should be at full Willpower for the next session.<br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T22:25:23-07:00","id":1392123,"title":"","content":"Honestly, as someone who hopes to be able to either play or masterize a Demon the Descent game soon(ish), your work here is amazing ! Keep it up please !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:10:12-07:00","id":1392233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1386630-actual-play-oklahoma-demons-session-1?p=1392123#post1392123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, as someone who hopes to be able to either play or masterize a Demon the Descent game soon(ish), your work here is amazing ! Keep it up please !</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. To be honest, I have no idea if anyone reads this, so your comment is very welcome. <br /> <br /> The <a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615\" target=\"_blank\">campaign website </a>has write-ups on a lot of the locations and characters as well. Basically you can know whatever the players know. See if you can figure out what is happening before the players do!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:33:12-07:00","id":1392839,"title":"","content":"Session 5 Notes: This was a rather important session. The players learned a lot of things, including the danger of plugging a 110V appliance into a 220V outlet. Link to the <a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/notes/29662\" target=\"_blank\">Session Notes. </a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 783px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Name</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Virtue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Vice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Aspirations</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Solomon Tzengeti</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Investigate Carlburton Inc.</li> <li>Protect a ring mate</li> <li>work on secondary cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Zachariah Ross (Mr. Zets)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Patient</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build something.</li> <li>Experience the loss of something.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Reginald Waters (EM)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Establish a 2nd cover;</li> <li>Acquire information useful for ring with mission;</li> <li>Engage in social interaction to further establish present cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Jennifer Reddings (Query)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Thorough</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build and use a new tool,</li> <li>Acquire criminal Experience for a future Cover,</li> <li>Figure out how to use the aether infused ink</li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Ring had returned to Norman, Oklahoma. Lexis had shifts to make up at The Grind, as well as practice sessions with Ramshackle Satire. The others planned to investigate a few leads. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> Solomon used his computer skills to find out what he could on Carlburton Inc. It turned out to be a small company located in Oklahoma City, only founded a little less that two years ago. It owned several other small companies involved with agriculture, freight, and oil drilling. Solomon managed to get a list of employees, and one name &quot;Helena Rogers&quot; stood out - she was in charge of Human Resources. Could this be the &quot;HR&quot; in the email they had found at Watchmaker Publications?<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The four made their plan: Reginald would approach Helena as she walked into her office building. He would explain that as a therapist he had a background in working with small companies on handling employee stress and job satisfaction. While he did that, Solomon would activate his <i>Mind Reading</i> Form ability. This would only require line of sight, so Solomon could sit safely in the parking lot. His goal was to find out what was the goal of the project Rogers was working on for The GodMachine. This would require a deeper dive than just reading surface thoughts. <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">On Tuesday morning they implemented their plan. Reginald arrived by separate car, Jennifer and Solomon sat together in Zets's car, while Zach observed separately from a park bench beside the reservoir in front of the office building. Reginald carefully timed his approach to intercept Helena at the door, and put on his best, most persuasive smile as he introduced himself. <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Helena was definitely interested in his services - would he join her to discuss this in her office?<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">This was <b>not</b> according to the plan! Waters had to keep her here in view of Solomon for the mind reading to work. Reginald turned up the charm to the maximum and deflected the offer, turning it into a conversational ploy to keep Helena standing there. He succeeded dramatically, and she put down her suitcase for a moment to chat.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon's eyes turned coppery as he activated his Form ability and reached out and... missed. He could not break through. He took a deep breath and tried again... contact! Now it was a matter of digging deep, hoping he could get the information he sought before Rogers went inside. He reached in and...<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Reginald saw Helena snap her head away to scan the area - as if she had the urgent need find someone. He tried to talk but she motioned for silence with her hand. <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon had gone rigid in the car, and then had started to shudder, drool starting to leak from the side of his mouth. Jennifer didn't know what had happened but this was clearly not good. Solomon felt as if he had reached into a mailbox to pull out a letter and something inside had grabbed his sleeve and was slowly, inexorably drawing his whole arm inside. He managed to break the contact before whatever had a hold of him could reel him in.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Still, he had managed to get some information. Helena was an Angel, part of a small team with a very special mission. The team was <i>not</i> affiliated with the Weather Centerbut was some sort of an experiment by The GodMachine. They were to accomplish some... very dangerous project. It was sufficiently dangerous that there had been three previous angels given this task but all three had failed to succeed within the mission parameters. The Farm provided one of the materials necessary for this occult matrix. Solomon had a sense that Rogers felt <i>proud</i>, that this was an unusual opportunity for an angel to show initiative, and that she was glad to be part of the team. However, he was unable to determine exactly what the project <i>was. </i>But in making contact with the angel, his Cover had been damaged.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Rogers made her excuses, breaking off the conversation, and hurried inside. It is not clear exactly what she had gathered from the interaction. Puzzled, Waters walked to his car and left. Zach stayed a while to avoid the appearance of a mass exodus, and then also left. <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Later that day Zach went to find someone at the university who could help him decipher the markings on the map. Lexis had identified the lines as ley lines, but the numerical markings at many different spots were a mystery. He was directed to Prof. Xincheng Shu, a petroleum geologist. He studied the map and after time became increasingly agitated. What he saw on the map was indications of drilling, illegal drilling, and possible extremely dangerous behavior. He asked to make a copy of the map and promised to meet with Zach on Wednesday after making some calls.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Shu phoned Ross early on Wednesday. The map indicated hydraulic fracturing in an area that was connected to the New Madrid fault. The New Madrid fault system was the source of one of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1811%E2%80%9312_New_Madrid_earthquakes\" target=\"_blank\">strongest earthquakes in North America</a> in recorded history. &quot;Frakking&quot; in this area would be incredibly risky. He asked to meet that morning in his office, and he would show Zach exactly what the map showed and where it was occurring.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">On arriving at the PetroGeology Department, Zach found Shu's hallway cordoned off by police tape. Apparently someone had murdered Shu in his office. The rumors were that it had been a crazy graduate student, but details were unclear. Ross tried to gain access to the office to see if he could get Shu's notes, but was prevented from entering the crime scene. As the crowd milled about a <i>truly</i> odd thing occurred.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A bizarre figure entered the hallway, a human being with mechanical modifications. This was clearly a Weatherman, and agent of the Weather Center. He seemed to be taking stock, carefully inspecting the crowd. No one - not police, students or faculty - took any notice of the figure. He seemed invisible to them. Zach copied the behavior of those around him. The figure inspected the crowd as if looking for someone or something. After minute or two the odd figure ambled over to a blackboard, picked up a piece of chalk, and wrote in large, shaky letters: &quot;SHAMAN'S PORTAL&quot;. It then left.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">That night, Solomon reflected on his close call as he brushed his teeth and prepared for bed. As he switched off the lights in the bathroom, an odd gleam caught his eye. He turned on the light - nothing. He turned off the light and found the source - it was his own eyes. <i>They now had a faint, permanent coppery glow,<br /> visible in darkness...</i><br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Game Notes:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Solomon suffered a Compromise from using an Exploit in the presence of an Angel. He acquired a permanent, minor glitch.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Jennifer and Solomon renew their Willpower by fulfilling their Virtues.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Reginald and Solomon gain Beats. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Jennifer, Solomon, Reginald and Zachariah gain one experience point.</span><br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:10:59-07:00","id":1392875,"title":"","content":"Wow, you've got some dedicated players ! My group seems to be a lot more harder to gather !I'm a little jealous to be honest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T13:14:44-07:00","id":1392887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1386630-actual-play-oklahoma-demons-session-1?p=1392875#post1392875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, you've got some dedicated players ! My group seems to be a lot more harder to gather !I'm a little jealous to be honest</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is on Discord, if that makes a difference. We play for about two hours in a session so it is not an onerous commitment. I posted on the Discord server to get players and it took about a week to get a group together. One person brought in two friends which might also have helped. <br /> <br /> <br /> Don\u2019t give up - there are a lot of people online looking for a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:53:31-07:00","id":1397384,"title":"","content":"Below are the notes for Session Six. I am a session behind (tonight will be session eight!). These are taking a bit longer to write up than I had expected. I apologize if it is poorly edited. The notes below are at the <a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/notes/31010\" target=\"_blank\">campaign session log</a>, which I will proofread at a later date. The campaign website also has images and hyperlinks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 783px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Name</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Virtue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Vice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Aspirations</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Solomon Tzengeti</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Investigate Carlburton Inc.</li> <li>Protect a ring mate</li> <li>work on secondary cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Zachariah Ross (Mr. Zets)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Patient</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build something.</li> <li>Experience the loss of something.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Reginald Waters (EM)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Establish a 2nd cover;</li> <li>Acquire information useful for ring with mission;</li> <li>Engage in social interaction to further establish present cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Jennifer Reddings (Query)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Thorough</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build and use a new tool,</li> <li>Acquire criminal Experience for a future Cover,</li> <li>Figure out how to use the aether infused ink</li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Game Note: Lexis Staiffer's player withdrew from the game for personal reasons. Their character was given a reason for the hiatus within the context of the game, in case they decide to return. (See below). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The section with Zets is long and wordy because it is based on text exchanges between the player and the storyteller. Impatient readers should skip the the section marked &quot;Back to table-play.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Solomon, Reginald, Jennifer and Lexis met on Thursday morning at the Wafflehousefor their regular weekly conversation with Mr. Gone. Reginald retrieved yet another burner phone hidden in the newspaper vending machine, as usual. Zachariah was not present, which was unusual. The four updated Mr. Gone on their adventures over the past week. Solomon asked if there was any other group that could take over this operation, since it really wasn't their purview. Mr. Gone explained that there were few Demon rings in this part of the country and anyone brought in to the area would need their own backstory to be established first. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Earlier that morning Zachariah gone out to pick up bagels for breakfast. His partner, Matty was there for breakfast - Lawrence was sleeping over at a friends house the night before. Upon his return, he found the apartment quiet - too quiet. In the kitchen he found Matty gagged and duct-taped to a chair. There was fear in her eyes. Beside her sat a man with a carving knife in one hand and a mug of coffee in the other. He smiled and spoke: &quot;Mr. Ross, I would like to chat with you about a trip you took last weekend in a rented SUV.&quot; He paused. &quot;Good coffee, by the way.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Zach activated the Embed <i>Cool Heads Prevail</i>. He ignored the stranger for several moments as he pulled out a cigarette and lit it. He calmly inhaled, and exhaled the smoke as he kept his profile to the Stranger. \u201cThat voice . . . I thought they would have put you away for longer. Good conduct?\u201d Zets glanced at Matty and will tap his forehead with his finger. \u201cAh, forgive me, dear. I often forget you dislike my habits. I will open a window. Frischen Luft, I suppose, would do us all good.\u201d Zets moved towards the window.<br /> <br /> On the table was a manila folder with papers in it. Slipping out of the folder was a dash-cam photo of the SUV Zets had rented for the Ring. It was a snapshot of it pulling away from vandalized church, taken from the perspective of the police car.<br /> <br /> The stranger smiled slightly, and ran a finger down Matty's face. &quot;She does seem to be the complaining type. &quot; He straightened up. &quot;No, this is a professional call. My employer has some very specific questions she would like answered. However...&quot; , he stopped for a moment to hold up the knife, sighting down the blade to examine its sharpness &quot;I may be able to combine business with pleasure.&quot; He smiled again and held the knife near Matty. &quot;So perhaps you can explain to me what you were doing in Elohim City? And who was the young woman behind the wheel of your rented SUV?&quot;<br /> <br /> Zets opened the window, inhaled another lungful of the scented smoke, then huff edit out into the outside air. He carefully got down a glass and a bottle of scotch, drawing out activity as he poured himself a glass. \u201cI wasn\u2019t certain what kind of bagel you preferred. I hope sesame is to your liking. You seem a sesame sort.\u201d Zets will tapped the ashes into a nearby ashtray. Du \u201cNever cared for it myself. Neither of us do. So take care and try not to spill the seeds about the place.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Stranger smiled. &quot;In my hobby... well profession now, I suppose, it is never a good idea to leave behind little clues. &quot; Zets noticed a canvas duffel bag on the floor containing a bottle of bleach, a box of plastic bags, and latex gloves. &quot;What were you doing in Elohim City? Who was driving the SUV?&quot;<br /> <br /> Zets will continued to gaze out the window, the cigarette hovering near his mouth as the smoke drifted from the tip. \u201cFor the moment, I will speak plainly. If you\u2019d like to discuss personal matters, you have me at a disadvantage. However, will ask that you conduct yourself, going forward, with a modicum of propriety and restraint.\u201d<br /> <br /> Zets face remains calm as he wondered why his Embed had failed. Perhaps, it was simply that the Stranger's head <i>was </i>cool. This was not the violence of passion, but of dry desire. He decided to stall for time.<br /> <br /> &quot;Research. Interviews. Gathering evidence and testimony to see what could be of use in a civil trial. But surely there are easier ways to gather this information?&quot; Zets sighed, with an ounce of drama. &quot;As for the girl? I scarcely know her. A guide, recommended to me by a colleague. I'm sure you are aware of just how insular these communities can be.<br /> <br /> The Stranger paused, considering this answer. He pauses to pluck a single strand of hair from Matty's head, causing her to flinch. &quot;A name, please?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Lizzy,&quot; Zets answered. &quot;That is how she was introduced to me, and that is how she introduced herself. I asked if it was short for Elizabeth, but that only earned me a smile. I could tell immediately, from her expression, posture, tone of voice, that further inquiry would yield no more.&quot; Zets sipped his scotch. &quot;So, tell me, for how long have you been corporate?<br /> <br /> &quot;Only very recently... In fact, it was a bit of a surprise. My employer contacted me and convinced me that they were aware of my.... work experience. In return for a hefty sum, and an assurance of not informing the police of certain facts, I agreed to discuss a few things with you.<br /> <br /> Now, I cannot believe that a man of your intelligence would rent an expensive vehicle for a total stranger. I want 'Lizzy's' full name and contact information. &quot;<br /> <br /> Zets calmly pulled a small notebook from his inner suit pocket, along with a pen. He wrote down the address of Marcy May Beeman. &quot;I can give you an address. Even this, I only ascertained through deduction.&quot; Zets placed the paper face down on the table. &quot;There is no reason why we cannot have a cordial relationship. We both understand the nature of business and information.&quot;<br /> <br /> Zets was hoping to avoid violence; however, as since this dids not seem possible, hel activated his Acidic Spit Form ability, spitting into the glass from which he was sipping. Since he has the merit Versatile Transformation, he also activated Blade Hand under his jacket. He tossed the acid into the Stranger's face, blinding him and causing searing pain that allowed Zets to finish him off with a single thrust. He restored his normal form, dragged the body into his Bolthole, and untied Matty.<br /> <br /> Zachariah had to spin a story for Matty - she had not seen his demonic Forms, only the effects that could be explained as mundane actions. He told a tale of a vengeful criminal he had helped convict, and hinted at a former life of intrigue and adventure. He assured her that he would take care of everything, but that for her safety, she needed to leave town for a few days while he made sure that all was indeed safe. Shaken, but moved by his heroism, she agreed.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Back to table play:</span></i><br /> <br /> As soon as practical, Zets showed up at the Wafflehouse. He showed them the folder of tracking information on the rental, as well as the photos of Lexis. &quot;Well shit, this is going to make things difficult.&quot; she sighed. Solomon pointed out that <i>she</i> was the only one in the photos because she had been alone when she encountered the sheriff. &quot;Look,&quot; she countered, &quot;this is a bit more than I signed up for. We were doing strictly surveillance. Then it became an investigation. Now it's getting way to frisky. I'm gonna take my band on the road for a while until this cools off.&quot; The others were unhappy with losing her, but respected her decision. She left to make arrangements.<br /> <br /> The remaining four tried to sort out what to investigate. After much discussion they decided that they would return to Talking Trees Camp Ground and see if they could track down the source of the Aether that had created the Hive Bear. Aether usually meant Infrastructure, so there had to be something there. Jennifer promised to call in a friend, a Cryptid expert. This expert might be able to help them track down the source of the Aether.<br /> <br /> The four drove out to Talking Trees Camp Ground, and there they met Tamir Lopez, Jennifer's contact. A strong, compact, outdoorsy character, Lopez eyed Jennifer's companions with suspicion. Lopez knew cryptids and she knew demons and she knew which she preferred. However, she was here as a favor to Query, paying off an old debt. Lopez explained that a cryptid the size of a Hive Bear needed a substantial amount of Aether, and that without Aether, it would slowly starve to death. She didn't like the idea of killing cryptids, but the insectile ones were often uncontrollable. Whatever intelligence they developed, it was too alien to tame or bargain with. However, she would help the track down the source of the Aether.<br /> <br /> She retrieved a large aluminum thermos from the front seat of her pick up. She opened it, and a thick black smoke poured forth on to the ground, gradually taking on the shape of a large dog. It had the size, shape, and apparent demeanor of a golden retriever, but formed from a thick roiling black vapor. Lopez gave the command, and the creature snapped alert, nosing the ground. It soon sped off into the woods, with the five following behind.<br /> <br /> The smoke hound soon led them down a rutted road that looked increasingly dubious. Then they found it: a delivery truck that had somehow taken a wrong turn and followed the same path some time ago. It was pitched over on its side, heavily damaged and clearly abandoned. It was marked Pandora Trucking.<br /> <br /> Carefully searching the truck revealed many broken glass jars - only two large jars were left intact. They held a viscous black fluid. Checking the manifest left in the cab of the truck the group found that it was from SunGold Honey, an outfit located in North Texas. The jars, when handled, induced an odd sensation of emitting a steady hot dry wind, as if from a blowdryer on low. There was no such wind - it was simply a sensation to those who were psychically sensitive. Solomon impulsively tried to taste it...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF9900\"><i>Death. Sickeningly sweet. Hot, dry, Death. Blood on the sand, Blood soaking into the sun-baked earth and exhaled as hot, dry Death. Death.</i></span><br /> <br /> This was the source of the Aether that had generated the cryptids. There was no standing Infrastructure, but rather some occult material to be used in a matrix, a material charged with Essence, Aether, and some sort of magical charge. The truck had tipped over here and attracted indigenous black bears. Now that the source of Aether was gone, any remaining Hive Bear(if there were any) would slowly starve.<br /> <br /> The manifest indicated that the truck was on the way to the Farm in Elohim City. But what would the Farm do with the honey? That was clearly the next step in the investigation.<br /> <br /> Lopez departed and the Ring debated their plans. They decided the simplest plan was perhaps the best: since tonight was a moonless night, they would simply fly or teleport in under there cover of darkness and see exactly what was going on. Solomon insisted on wearing a balaclava and a stocking over his face - he was not going to make the same mistake Lexis had!<br /> <br /> That night the four parked their rented SUV in the woods near the Farm. Those who could fly scouted the area, giving directions to those who could not. Luckily, no one failed their Compromise roll. <i><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(Partial transformations).</span></i><br /> <br /> The Farm has only one entrance, a dirt road branching off from the single cross street in Elohim CIty. Located roughly a quarter mile from the city, The Farm consisted of several fenced in pastures, an unusually large warehouse-like building, and eight to ten smaller buildings including bunkhouses, a garage and a small church. The area did not resemble the aerial maps on Google maps or Google Earth. Located in this undeveloped area where the border between Arkansas and Oklahoma is ill-defined it was in a bit of a legal no-man\u2019s land. It was hard to approach from other directions, with the nearest road to the east about ten miles away through scrub pines and marsh.<br /> <br /> The area was patrolled by three or four heavily armed groups - militia types in hunter's camouflage. Keeping to the skies, the Demons were unseen. The Ring communicated in short, agreed upon phrases over burner phones with hands-free head sets. They agreed to convene on the top of the large warehouse.<br /> <br /> The building was odd - there were no windows, and only the large doors at one end as an entrance. The Ring looked for vents or holes, but the interior seemed to lined with a dark cloth that obscured the view from anyone who might want to, say, look inside to teleport. As they waited, the doors to the warehouse opened, and disgorged its mysterious contents.<br /> <br /> It was a herd of cows - milk-white was hardly the word to describe them. The were pure white, almost phosphorescent in the moonless night. Their eyes were milk-white as well. They were accompanied by their own special armed guard as they were lead out to a pasture to feed. After they had left the area, Query decided that they would also activate their Mirror-Skin Form, spending Aether to transform back to Cover and then additional Aether to active both Flight and Mirror Skin. They teleported down to investigate the inside of the warehouse.<br /> <br /> The walls and ceiling of the warehouse were lined with thick black cloth. Inside the warehouse was yet another, smaller building, which again had no windows. The doorway to the smaller building faced in the opposite direction to that of the larger. Query investigated, his Mirror Skin keeping him from sight. The smaller building was simply a barn for holding the cows that they had just seen. There was food and water for the animals, as well as some milking equipment. Query felt that the aura from the small amounts of milk left in one bucket matched the &quot;feel&quot; of the aura radiated by the ink at Watchmaker Publications.<br /> <br /> What was the link between these discoveries - milk and honey? What part did they play in the occult matrix that The GodMachine was building? Did the Farm feed the honey to the cows, or was this something different?<br /> <br /> Query decided to investigate further....</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24502,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","user":"KieranMullen","date":".  Fixed terribly spacing! 06-27-2020, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T21:22:22-07:00","id":1399200,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Characters Present:</b></u></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 768px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Name</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Virtue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Vice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Aspirations</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Solomon Tzengeti</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Investigate Carlburton Inc.</li> <li>Protect a ring mate</li> <li>work on secondary cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Zachariah Ross (Mr. Zets)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Patient</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build something.</li> <li>Experience the loss of something.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Reginald Waters (EM)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Passionate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Cruel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Establish a 2nd cover;</li> <li>Acquire information useful for ring with mission;</li> <li>Engage in social interaction to further establish present cover</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Jennifer Reddings (Query)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Curious</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">Thorough</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\"><ul><li>Build and use a new tool,</li> <li>Acquire criminal Experience for a future Cover,</li> <li>Figure out how to use the aether infused ink</li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> <br /> What was the link between these discoveries - milk and honey? What part did they play in the occult matrix that The GodMachine was building? Did the Farm feed the honey to the cows, or was this something different? <br /> <br /> Query, partially transformed and cloaked in Mirrorskin, decided to investigate The Farm further. His attention was drawn to the small church nearby, in which lights flickered. Approaching carefully he found that it was a rather old wooden building with a shiny new coat of white paint. It was generally featureless like many Protestant churches from the turn of the century. It did not have stained glass windows - just plain ones. In gold letters over the door is was written \u201c<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><i>Deus Machina Vult</i></span>\u201d. He looked through a window that was dirty, but clean enough to give him a view. There was some sort of ceremony going on inside, and there were about a dozen people attending. The door to the church was ajar, and the attention of the people inside was focussed on the ceremony in the front, so Query risked going inside. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Solomon activated his mind-reading Form ability and tried probing the sentries. He found nothing of particular interest, no connection to the honey, just a fanatic dedication to protected the unusual herd of cows. When Query had informed (via whispers on cell phones) that he was going in the church, Solomon teleported to the ground.<br /> <br /> The interior had a definite mechanical motif. All sorts of gears are nailed to the sides of the pews - bicycle gears, truck gears, etc. Golden gears were painted on the walls, at times these <i>painted images </i> seem to turn slowly. At the front of the church was an old fashioned copper bathtub, the kind seen in old westerns. There was also an altar and a pulpit. <br /> <br /> The tub was filled with milk from two large canisters, milk that had an odd glowing sheen to it. A cow and a young man stood beside the tub. The man climbed into the tub while the crowd chanted \u201c<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><i>Deus Machina Vult</i></span>\u201d. He was totally immersed as the cow's throat was slit, blood pouring into the tub which began to froth and glow. When the man emerged, he was changed. He now bore the incredibly bulked physique of the interlopers the Ring hand met back in Session 1. He was now one of the Moonblessed, his eyes changed to a milky white. He climbed out of the tub, took one look in the direction of Query, and sprang in a bellowing charge.<br /> <br /> The speed of his reaction surprised Query, and the two tumbled out the door in a wrestling tangle. The congregation poured out of the church to follow them. When Query had gathered his bearings he found himself trapped in a full Nelson headlock, and felt the transformed brute flex his muscles in a move to snap Query's neck. But teleportation is line of sight and requires but a thought, and Query popped out of the deadly embrace to appear a few dozen meters away. The Moonblessed roared, quickly locked on him again, and ran at Query. But with a few precious seconds to think Query picked a point on the edge of the forest and teleported to it. Then it took just a few minutes of sprinting and a few more random dashes to elude the pursuer. <br /> <br /> The rest of the Ring decided to leave while the going was good. Teleporting or flying, they made their way back to their SUV, and compared notes.<br /> <br /> A few days later Solomon want to consult one of his Contacts, an Exile named Sifrayah, who ran DawnWalker Bookstore in Boston. Using a special linking book, Solomon was able to step from a library stack into the bookstore located over a thousand miles away. Sifrayah was a gossip, and gave information to Angels and Demons alike. His original mission was to archive books for The GodMachine. To this day angels are unwilling to put an end to his store for fear that The GodMachinemight actually demand that they retrieve some arcane tome from him.<br /> <br /> Solomon asked Sifrayah about &quot;HR&quot; and learned that she was of middling ability and power. Her area of Influence was Human Resources: she could always find someone, somewhere, to do whatever job she needed doing. That might range from shifty truckers who would carry cargo without asking questions to murderous psychopaths willing to dispatch troubling investigators. Solomon asked Sifrayah to look into her Bans and Banes.<br /> <br /> Sifrayah was intrigued by the goings on in Oklahoma. He claimed that &quot;everyone knew&quot; that The GodMachine had some project that involved moving ley lines, and that it was so phenomenally dangerous that it lead to the disassembly of three previous angels who could not balance the conflicting priorities of the mission. The goal was to tap in to some of the energy in the ley lines, partially redirecting them. Of course, not even The GodMachine would be so foolish as to actually <i>disrupt</i> the ley lines since, well, that would lead to the <i>obvious</i> disaster. <br /> <br /> The Ring decided that their next target would be the final destination on thePandora Trucking shipping manifest. Where had they been taking the Blood Honey? What was being done with it? And what was the connection to the milk produced at The Farm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}